Done: Claude limits now come from yoagent 0.27.2, apart from two output-maximum rows that yoagent doesn't supply as data (below). The commit is 8cbfd42a, titled "Fixes #1144 (item 2), Part of #1121", so the push closes #1144. Build, clippy with -D warnings, fmt and the full cargo test run all passed.

What changed
• `/model info` window (commands_info::model_context_window): the Claude branch of the hand-written lookup table is gone. A Claude id now gets the window the agent is actually built with: its yoagent preset if it has one, else a Bedrock or OpenRouter preset, else anthropic_model_config, which uses 0.27.2's table and otherwise yoagent's 200K default. I checked the callers: /model info is the only production reader.
• Output ceiling (agent_builder::anthropic_output_maximum): it reads yoagent's table first, which covers Opus 4.7, 4.6 and 4.5. I kept two hand rows, claude-opus-5* and claude-haiku-5-5 at 128K, because yoagent only states those in doc comments, not as data. Without them, a user who sets max_tokens above 128K gets a 400 with no warning first.

Measured before → after

| id | window | output max |
|---|---|---|
| claude-sonnet-4-5 | 1M → 200K | None → None |
| claude-sonnet-4-20250514 | 1M → 200K | None → None |
| claude-opus-4-7 | 1M → 1M | None → 128000 |
| claude-opus-4-6 | 1M → 1M | None → 128000 |
| claude-opus-4-5 | 200K → 200K | None → 64000 |
| claude-zzz-9 (made up) | 200K → 200K | None → None |
| Bedrock anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 | 1M → 200K | not used |

Ids with a named preset didn't change. The old 1M values were the table guessing; the agent already ran at 200K for those ids. Sonnet 4 and Sonnet 4.5 have no yoagent row, so they get the 200K default.

Checks
• Probed from /tmp: --model claude-opus-4-5 --max-tokens 100000 printed no warning before and now prints "exceeds … declared output ceiling 64000". On the anthropic provider, claude-opus-4-6 and -4-7 print no guessed-limits warning.
• Tests (src/anthropic_preset_tests.rs):
  • Every offered Claude id, anthropic and Bedrock, reports the window create_model_config builds.
  • Every row in yoagent's anthropic table that states limits matches yoyo's output maximum and window.
  • Near-misses: claude-zzz-9, sonnet-4-5 and sonnet-4-20250514 get the default window, not 1M.
  • I broke each new test on purpose, saw it fail by name, and restored it.
• Existing `commands_info` tests: the old test that pinned where the hand table disagreed became hand_table_holds_no_claude_window. Three asserts that expected 1M for ids yoagent has no row for now expect 200K, with comments saying why.
• `tests/module_size.rs`: commands_info.rs is now 3558 lines (was 3576) and agent_builder.rs 4977 (was 4980). I lowered both limits there.
• Docs: none quoted a Claude window that changed.

