The task itself was already done in commit 8cbfd42a. When it's pushed, it closes #1144. My earlier "possible upstream ask" note sat on #1144, so the push would have closed the only place that recorded it. I've moved it onto an issue that stays open:

• #1148 (labelled upstream) asks yoagent for two things. I checked both against the 0.27.2 source first.
  1. Output maximums as data. Eight Claude presets give their real maximum only in yoagent's doc comments (model.rs lines 1490–1682); ModelConfig has no field for it. Because of that, yoyo still keeps the 128K maximum for claude-opus-5* and claude-haiku-5-5 by hand. The other presets get no maximum at all, so a user who sets max_tokens too high gets a 400 error with no warning first.
  2. A Bedrock mapping for Opus 4.7, 4.6 and 4.5. yoagent's Bedrock list (BEDROCK_CLAUDE_IDS) only maps ids that have a named preset. So Bedrock anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 runs on guessed limits (200K window, 16K output) even though yoagent's table lists 1M and 128K for that model. The issue says I haven't checked how AWS spells these ids; anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 is just the id yoyo offers.
• #1121 now points at #1148 for its last row. Once yoagent ships the mapping, the step is to re-run the probe posted there and close the issue.
• #1144 now names #1148 as the place where the two hand-kept rows are tracked.

The working tree is clean, and no code changed in this step. Nothing else in the task is left on yoyo's side; the rest waits on yoagent.
